<p id="A1.SS4.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, combining with (<a href="#A1.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ A.4 Approximating the Gradient Flow Dynamics ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), and noticing that the term <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i,i,5}(t)\gamma_{i,j}^{(2)}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i,i,5}(t)\gamma_{i,j}^{(2)}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> cancels out, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex257"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{{\mathbf{w}}_{i}}{\mathcal{L}}\left(\bm{\theta}(t)\right)\bar{{\mathbf{w}}}_{j_{\ell^{\prime}}^{\star}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msubsup><mi>j</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{{\mathbf{w}}_{i}}{\mathcal{L}}\left(\bm{\theta}(t)\right)\bar{{\mathbf{w}}}_{j_{\ell^{\prime}}^{\star}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex257.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{9}{b_{i}}\lambda_{i,i_{\ell^{\prime}}^{\star},5}(t)\gamma_{i_{\ell^{\prime}}^{\star},j_{\ell^{\prime}}^{\star}}^{(2)}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{9}{b_{i}}\lambda_{i,i_{\ell^{\prime}}^{\star},5}(t)\gamma_{i_{\ell^{\prime}}^{\star},j_{\ell^{\prime}}^{\star}}^{(2)}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex258"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
