<div id="A1.SS5.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout the proof, we will relax the upper bound in terms of <math id="A1.SS5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathcal{A},\ell}^{(1)}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathcal{A},\ell}^{(1)}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> into the upper bound in terms of <math id="A1.SS5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathcal{A},\ell}^{(2)}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathcal{A},\ell}^{(2)}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounding <math id="A1.SS5.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t),\zeta_{i,j}^{(2)}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t),\zeta_{i,j}^{(2)}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.SS5.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> First, we are going to derive some rough estimation for <math id="A1.SS5.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t),\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t),\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS5.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[m]\setminus\mathcal{R}_{\ell-1},j\in[m^{\star}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[m]\setminus\mathcal{R}_{\ell-1},j\in[m^{\star}]</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma7" title="Lemma 7. ‣ A.4 Approximating the Gradient Flow Dynamics ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we have that</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex381"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex381.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\left|\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\left|\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex381.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{a_{i}}\nabla_{{\mathbf{v}}_{i}}{\mathcal{L}}\left(\bm{\theta}(t)\right)^{\top}\bar{{\mathbf{w}}}_{j}^{\star}\cdot\text{sign}\left(\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>sign</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{a_{i}}\nabla_{{\mathbf{v}}_{i}}{\mathcal{L}}\left(\bm{\theta}(t)\right)^{\top}\bar{{\mathbf{w}}}_{j}^{\star}\cdot\text{sign}\left(\zeta_{i,j}^{(1)}(t)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex382"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
