<p id="A1.SS5.p16.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p16.5.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, by the definition of <math id="A1.SS5.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}_{i_{\ell}^{\star},j_{\ell}^{\star},1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}_{i_{\ell}^{\star},j_{\ell}^{\star},1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex457"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
